      "hints": [
        "Form $fg(x) = 2 - 3\\cos(\\frac{1}{2}x) = 1$.",
        "Solve $\\cos(\\frac{1}{2}x) = \\frac{1}{3} \\implies \\frac{1}{2}x \\approx 1.231$.",
        "$x \\approx 2.46$ rad."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Form the composite function $fg(x)$ and equate to 1:\n$$fg(x) = f\\left(\\frac{1}{2}x\\right) = 2 - 3\\cos\\left(\\frac{1}{2}x\\right) = 1$$",
        "Isolate $\\cos\\left(\\frac{1}{2}x\\right)$:\n$$3\\cos\\left(\\frac{1}{2}x\\right) = 1 \\implies \\cos\\left(\\frac{1}{2}x\\right) = \\frac{1}{3}$$\n$$\\frac{1}{2}x = \\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right) \\approx 1.2310 \\text{ radians}$$",
        "Solve for $x$ in the range $0 \\le x \\le 2\\pi$ (to 3 significant figures):\n$$x = 2 \\times 1.2310 \\approx 2.4619 \\approx 2.46 \\text{ radians} \\quad (\\text{or } \\approx 0.784\\pi)$$"
      ],
